  "summary_en": "Oregon enrolled House Bill 4127 (2024) protects warehouse distribution center workers by requiring written disclosure of productivity quotas, barring discipline for undocumented quotas, and giving employees a right to request their work speed data. It sets civil penalties enforced by the Bureau of Labor and Industries. It does not mention AI or robots.",
  "key_provisions_or_claims": [
   "Employers must give written quota documentation, including consequences of missing it.",
   "No adverse action for failing a quota that was not documented.",
   "Employees can request 90 days of work speed data within 21 days, free of charge.",
   "Violations of the records right bring civil penalties up to $1,000.",
   "Collective bargaining agreements with equivalent rights are exempt."
  ],
